  <span class="eyebrow">For ICF Coaches</span>
  <h1>TRE™ Training with <em>ICF CCEs</em></h1>
  <p>21 ICF CCEs from one course: learn a somatic self-regulation practice for yourself, and count the hours towards your ACC, PCC or MCC renewal.</p>
</div><section class="section-cream">
  <div class="answer-box">
    <span class="k">In one line</span>
    <p>TRE™ Module 1 with Isabelle Claus Teixeira is an ICF-accredited course worth <strong style="color:var(--gold)">21 CCEs</strong> (16 Resource Development + 5 Core Competencies). You learn a somatic self-regulation practice for yourself, and the hours count towards renewing your ACC, PCC or MCC credential. (CCEs were formerly called CCEUs.)</p>
  </div>
</section><section class="section-white">
  <div class="section-header-center">
    <span class="section-eyebrow">For Coaches</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Why a <em>Somatic Tool</em> Belongs in Coaching</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="gd">
    <p>Coaching asks clients to think clearly, notice patterns and choose new actions. That is hard to do when the nervous system is stuck in stress. More and more coaches are adding body-based practices so that clients — and the coach — can settle before they think.</p>
    <p>TRE™ is one of the simplest of these practices. It needs no equipment and no talking about the past, and once learned it becomes a self-care practice you can use for the rest of your life. Module 1 starts with you: your own regulation, your own presence in the room.</p>
    <h3>What you take away</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>A reliable way to come back to calm between demanding sessions.</li>
      <li>Greater presence and steadier attention with clients.</li>
      <li>First-hand understanding of how stress lives in the body.</li>
      <li>A clear path to offering TRE™ to clients later, through Modules 2 and 3.</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section><section class="section-cream">
  <div class="section-header-center">
    <span class="section-eyebrow">The Course</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">What Module 1 <em>Covers</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-grid">
    <div class="tile"><i class="fa-solid fa-brain"/><h3>The neuroscience</h3><p>How neurogenic tremoring works and why it helps the nervous system release stress.</p></div>
    <div class="tile"><i class="fa-solid fa-person-running"/><h3>The TRE™ sequence</h3><p>The full exercise sequence, practised and refined with direct feedback.</p></div>
    <div class="tile"><i class="fa-solid fa-hand-holding-heart"/><h3>Self-regulation</h3><p>Somatic awareness, containment and grounding, so you can practise safely on your own.</p></div>
    <div class="tile"><i class="fa-solid fa-mug-hot"/><h3>Self-care for coaches</h3><p>A session on self-care and presence for coaches, opening the training.</p></div>
    <div class="tile"><i class="fa-solid fa-laptop"/><h3>Personal sessions</h3><p>In Singapore, Module 1 also includes four individual online TRE™ sessions to deepen your practice.</p></div>
    <div class="tile"><i class="fa-solid fa-award"/><h3>Certificate</h3><p>Valid as Module 1 of the Global TRE™ Provider Certification, recognised worldwide.</p></div>
  </div>
</section><section class="section-white">
  <div class="section-header-center">
    <span class="section-eyebrow">Credential Renewal</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">How the CCEs <em>Count</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="gd">
    <p>ICF credentials (ACC, PCC and MCC) are renewed every three years with continuing coach education. CCEs are split into <strong>Core Competencies</strong> (directly about coaching skills) and <strong>Resource Development</strong> (knowledge and tools that support your coaching).</p>
    <p>Every three years you need <strong>40 CCEs</strong>: at least <strong>24 in Core Competencies</strong> (including 3 in Coaching Ethics), and up to <strong>16 in Resource Development</strong>.</p>
    <p>TRE™ Module 1 gives you <strong>16 Resource Development</strong> CCEs — your full Resource Development allowance for a cycle — plus <strong>5 Core Competency</strong> CCEs. That is more than half of a renewal from a single course. Keep your certificate of completion: you will need it when you log your hours with ICF.</p>
    <p style="font-size:.88rem;color:var(--text-mid)">Renewal rules are set by ICF and can change. Check the current requirements on <a href="https://coachingfederation.org/credentialing/renew-your-credential/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ICF’s renewal page</a>.</p>
  </div>
</section><section class="section-cream">
  <div class="section-header-center">
    <span class="section-eyebrow">Upcoming</span>
    <h2 class="section-title">Module 1 <em>Dates</em></h2>
  </div>
  <div class="tile-grid" style="grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr);max-width:820px">
    <a class="tile" href="/event-certification-2027" style="text-decoration:none"><i class="fa-solid fa-location-dot"/><h3>Singapore · 24–25 April 2027</h3><p>Module 1 of the 2027 certification cohort. 21 ICF CCEs with the Growth Package.</p></a>
    <a class="tile" href="/event-tre-module1-lisbon" style="text-decoration:none"><i class="fa-solid fa-location-dot"/><h3>Lisboa · 28–30 May 2027</h3><p>Three days in Lisbon, Portugal; the 21 ICF CCEs require the additional 4-hour Self-Care &amp;amp; Presence for Coaches session (Day 3, 14:00–18:00). 25 places. Early bird €739 until 31 March 2027.</p></a>
  </div>
